rganization Location & Map Introduction Director General and Deputy Director Generals Contact Us Overseas Offices News & Press Releases News Events Announcement Chinese 中文 Contact Informationmenu-wrap ::: Import and export related laws and regulations Import & Export Regulations/Guidelines Announcement about the"Guidelines for Labeling the Origin of Specific Imported Textiles" (Refer to Annex), effective May 18, 2023. 2023-04-28 Announcement by the Bureau of Foreign Trade, Ministry of Economic Affairs Date: April 28, 2023 Document No.: Mao Fu 1120150959 Subject: Announcement about the"Guidelines for Labeling the Origin of Specific Imported Textiles" (Refer to Annex), effective May 18, 2023. Legal Basis: Articles 11 and 20 of the Regulations Governing the Import of Commodities Supplementary Information: In order to coordinate amendments to both the"Labeling Criteria for Apparel and Garments" and"Labeling Criteria for Textiles" as announced by the Ministry of Economic Affairs (MOEA), the Bureau of Foreign Trade (BOFT) publicly announces the aforementioned guidelines. The announcement about Doc. No. Mao Fu 09670224750 issued by the BOFT on Nov. 2, 2007 shall cease to apply, effective May 18, 2023. Director General Cynthia Kiang CTR： 1730 Attachment Guidelines for Labeling the Origin of Specific Imported Textiles 20230518.odt Guidelines for Labeling the Origin of Specific Imported Textiles 20230518.pdf This website provides users with different formats of documents.Please install the free and open software provided , if the document is in the “odf” format.You may also open it with your customary software. Back ::: Sitemap Expanded Sourcing from Taiwan Digital Trade Feature Service Overseas Services Trade Financing Trade Relations Multilateral Trade Bilateral Trade FTAs Trade Remedy Cases New Southbound MICE Industry MICE Advantages MICE Facilities Trade Law & Administration Trade Law Registration of Exporters and Importers Import & Export Administration CITES Certificat